    "description": "Nigeria's first presidential election since independence, held on 11 August 1979 after more than a decade of military rule, with five parties contesting. Shehu Shagari of the NPN won a 33.77% plurality of the 16,846,533 valid votes, ahead of Obafemi Awolowo (UPN) and Nnamdi Azikiwe (NPP), and was declared elected by FEDECO; the Supreme Court later upheld his win in Awolowo v Shagari over the two-thirds-of-states threshold. State figures are reported as percentage shares only — no per-state vote counts were published — so each state row shows the winning party and its share. Bendel and Gongola are the 19-state boundaries of the time and have no modern polygon."
